# HIST-36: Navigation history survives process death, without the saved view
# state.
#
# launch-task, not launch-view. The trail is per session and is never written to
# storage, which HIST-37 pins by asserting a fresh VIEW intent starts empty. It
# comes back here only because resuming the task restores the activity from its
# saved instance state. Using launch-view would assert the opposite of what the
# app does and fail for the wrong reason.
describe Navigation history survives process death, without the saved view state

# Builds the trail: Go To Page 9, zoom above 1.0, Go To Page 17, then
# backgrounds the app.
phase com.gitlab.mudlej.MjPdfReader.suite.history.History36ProcessDeathTest#phaseOneBuildTrailAndBackground

kill-app
# Phase-two instrumentation must start before the task is brought forward;
# otherwise Orchestrator force-stops the restored activity during startup.
launch-task-after-start

# Asserts three history rows with their origin labels, and that tapping Page 9
# lands on index 8 and keeps the restored current zoom, because restored entries
# carry no view state.
phase com.gitlab.mudlej.MjPdfReader.suite.history.History36ProcessDeathTest#phaseTwoAssertTrailRestored
